Phase 8 item 6 (managed Postgres + S3 bindings) — object-store binding proof
Date: 2026-09-13

SCOPE: the S3 binding half of item 6 (the Postgres adapter slice follows).
ObjectStore seam in crates/event-store: ONE contract, three backends —
SqliteObjectStore (today's semantics, default), LocalFsObjectStore
(content-addressed atomic files), S3ObjectStore (minimal SigV4 signer
over hmac/sha2, path-style, payload-hash-signed). SigV4 verified end-to-end
against a REAL S3-compatible server (MinIO via docker, quay.io image,
127.0.0.1:9000): bucket create through the signer + the full contract
suite (round trip, digest verification, range clamp, replace, delete,
tenant/task namespacing isolation). Managed AWS S3 proper stays the
operator-gated credential boundary (TLS hop + real creds).
SEAM INTEGRATION: RuntimeStore::with_object_store routes NEW output-ref
payloads to the backend (SQL keeps preview+metadata only, asserted
inline length 0), reads come back digest-verified, legacy inline rows
still read; default (no backend) is byte-for-byte today's behavior.

